    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **280 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented AUDIT logging for successful owner creation in the OfficeFloor `POST /api/owners` pipeline.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `LogOwnerCreationAudit.java`:\n- Logs to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`.\n- Records the authenticated user (via `SecurityContextHolder`), the new owner's `id`, and `membershipNumber`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` (where the id is assigned) and `respond`, keeping it under the same `govern: [ transaction ]` span so it only runs on the success path.\n\nDesign notes:\n- I first tried the OfficeFloor tutorial pattern of injecting `UserDetails` as a function parameter, but this project's OfficeFloor/Spring bridge doesn't expose it for auto-wiring (context failed to load). Since the project logs `OfficeFloor bridging Spring Security` and propagates the security context to the function thread, `SecurityContextHolder.getContext().getAuthentication().getName()` correctly yields the authenticated user (`acceptance-admin` in the test).\n- Placing the step after `save` guarantees the DB-generated `id` is populated (the existing responder already relies on this).\n\nThe provided `Cp19Tests` passes, confirming the AUDIT log records the user and owner id, and the audit line \u2014 `AUDIT - owner created: user=acceptance-admin id=11 membershipNumber=11` \u2014 shows all three required fields.",
